Description: offline-first CLI for static credential exposure analysis
 CredScope is an experimental, offline-first command-line tool for
 analyzing static credential exposure and reachability context in
 Docker Compose files, GitHub Actions workflows, and imported Gitleaks
 JSON reports. It builds a typed graph of credentials, permissions,
 ports, mounts, and service dependencies, then scores and reports the
 findings in terminal, HTML, JSON, SARIF 2.1.0, or Mermaid format.
 .
 CredScope performs deterministic static analysis only. It does not
 validate whether discovered credentials are active, execute repository
 content, or make network requests, and it is not a replacement for a
 complete vulnerability scanner or for Gitleaks. Findings should not be
 the sole basis for a security decision.
